<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!-- Me = mod project. Guid, id, category come from file name. Build rules live in Directory.Build.props/.targets. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ModName>Cheated Tag Remover</ModName>
    <Version>0.1.0</Version>
    <ModScope>QoL</ModScope>
    <!-- No ModIdea: user asked for me direct, no row in the idea sheet. -->
    <!-- Both: whole world live only where world run (server, host), so dedicated server must load me too (Client mod
         never load there). No PlayerCheck: me = admin tool, players without me stay welcome. Client on server without
         me: command stay (made in BindConfig), clean own items and loaded area only. -->
    <ModSide>Both</ModSide>
    <ModMultiplayer>Compatible</ModMultiplayer>
    <ModMultiplayerNotes>Install it where the world runs (the dedicated server, or the player who hosts) to clean the whole world, and on the game of the admin who types the command. Other players do not need it; those who have it also get the items they carry cleaned. On a server without it, the command only cleans your own items and what is loaded around you.</ModMultiplayerNotes>
    <!-- Wire format (bump when it change). Peer rpc, one string each, first field = layout "1":
           client -> server  "<guid>.Request"  "1|clear" or "1|scan"   admin ask for the world pass
           server -> client  "<guid>.Local"    "1|clear"               clean own items and objects you own, now
           server -> client  "<guid>.Reply"    "1|<text lines>"        answer for the admin who asked
         No ZDO key of me own: me only write vanilla keys (cheated, cheatedQueued, items, itemData). -->
    <ModNetworkVersion>1</ModNetworkVersion>
    <ModRequires></ModRequires>
    <ModDescription>Console commands that remove the vanilla cheated tag from a whole world: building pieces, creatures, stations, items in chests, on the ground and on stands, and the items you carry. Nothing is deleted.</ModDescription>
    <!-- Decision (2026-10-17): me stay out of 1.0 release and all-mods pack until me reworked for Valheim 1.0.20.
         Package-Mod skip me (no page, no tag, not in pack). Me still build, deploy and run tests like others.
         Me keep 0.x Version: no 1.0.0 bump with the others; me first real release = 1.0.0 later.
         Framework refusal-screen code (2026-10-17) also in my dll since then. Me not shipped, so no bump for it now:
         rework version note it in CHANGELOG. -->
    <ModShip>false</ModShip>
    <ModShipNote>Needs a rework for Valheim 1.0.20, which changed how the game stores the cheated tag (see the README). Left out of the 1.0 release and the all-mods pack until then.</ModShipNote>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
